wrote:

> Is it worth doing some more sacrificing to improve my luck before
> donating?  Will that give me a chance of more protection points?  

I think (but I'm not entirely sure) that getting protection from
donating, even the first lot, is completely independent from luck; the
x points on the first donation is entirely random, the next (9-x) are
guaranteed (one at a time until you're at intrinsic 1); after that it's
a 1 in (10 - current intrinsic AC) chance, again entirely random, until
you max out at -10.

> I've 
> seen three or four clovers so far, but that luck might have timed out,
> which will still happen with an unblessed luckstone, won't it?

No, an uncursed luckstone fixes luck, good or bad, without ever timing
out. Your luck is unchanged unless *you* do something to change it,
like sacrificing. You don't need extra luck for getting protection, but
it may be nice to have it regardless. If you bless your luckstone, bad
luck times out (to 1, because the luckstone gives you an extra point of
luck) and good luck doesn't. With a cursed luckstone everything is
reversed: good luck times out to -1 and bad luck doesn't.

> Am I right in believing that there's not
> necessarily a teleport trap (in an "ad aurarium", or however it's
> spelt, cupboard) for each vault?  

"ad aerarium", usually scuffed a bit. You're right in believing that not
all vaults have one; also, especially on deeper levels, a trap marked
"ad aerarium" may be a level teleporter instead.

> I've not found one yet, and have 
> failed to note which levels have vaults.  Any hints for locating them
> without the cupboard or magic mapping or random digging?  This is the
> first time I've really wanted to find them *right now* as against if I
> get the chance later.

Object detection. Nymphs tend to carry potions of same. Or gold
detection, of course, though you may want to save your scrolls of gold
detection for when you *really* need them to detect other things than
gold. Or look for a large area that seems to be empty and dig there.

